  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "Evidence: Only one experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) has been completed, yielding ~48.5% accuracy. This gives us almost no information about which design dimensions matter. The most fundamental question for a multimodal cellular profiling study is whether adding the image modality provides any benefit over RNA-only. Question: Does multimodal fusion (adding resnet50 image features via concat) improve validation accuracy over the RNA-only baseline? config_016 keeps the RNA side identical to config_001 (pca_n2000, singleprofile) and adds the simplest, most standard image setup (resnet50, concat fusion), cleanly isolating the effect of the image modality. Why this is the best next step: With only one data point, the highest-uncertainty decision is whether multimodal is worth pursuing at all. A positive result justifies investing remaining budget in fusion strategies, image encoder choices, and multiprofile aggregation within the multimodal space. A negative result redirects effort toward RNA-encoder and profile-setting improvements. No other single experiment reduces uncertainty about this pivotal design choice as efficiently."
}

